// Title: LSASS Dump Keyword In CommandLine
// ID: ffa6861c-4461-4f59-8a41-578c39f3f23e
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: E.M. Anhaus, Tony Lambert, oscd.community, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-10-24
// Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1003.001
// Description: Detects the presence of the keywords "lsass" and ".dmp" in the commandline, which could indicate a potential attempt to dump or create a dump of the lsass process.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

_sourceCategory=* | where (((CommandLine matches "*lsass.dmp*" or CommandLine matches "*lsass.zip*" or CommandLine matches "*lsass.rar*" or CommandLine matches "*Andrew.dmp*" or CommandLine matches "*Coredump.dmp*" or CommandLine matches "*NotLSASS.zip*" or CommandLine matches "*lsass_2*" or CommandLine matches "*lsassdump*" or CommandLine matches "*lsassdmp*")) or ((CommandLine matches "*lsass*" and CommandLine matches "*.dmp*")) or ((CommandLine matches "*SQLDmpr*" and CommandLine matches "*.mdmp*")) or ((CommandLine matches "*nanodump*" and CommandLine matches "*.dmp*")))
